{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Amplitude","anchor":"Sending-to-Amplitude","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory throws "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its "},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, and its "},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no "},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". No "},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent. Its "},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with, into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Amplitude] …"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$identify"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$groupidentify"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/2\/httpapi"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","title":"BatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"title":"AmplitudeEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"title":"batchLimit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder\/batchlimit","fragments":[{"text":"static","